          %p
            The idea of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            is to study “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"}> spaces
            ” with “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"}> continuous functions
            ” between them. Specifically one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            (whence “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"}> point-set topology
            ”, see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#PointSetTopology"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuity
            is familiar from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Continuity"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSpace"}
            below).
          %p
            Hence,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            is the study of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            (see also remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopCategory"}
            below). This category is much more flexible than that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            of spaces. Accordingly, topology underlies or informs many and diverse areas of mathematics, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebra
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            theory, hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+rings"} local rings
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/low-dimensional+topology"} low-dimensional topology
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+domain+theory"} topological domain theory
          %p
            A popular imagery for the concept of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            is provided by deformations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elasticity"} elastic
            physical bodies, which may be deformed by stretching them without tearing. The canonical illustration is a continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijective
            function from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            to the surface of a coffee mug, which maps half of the torus to the handle of the coffee mug, and continuously deforms parts of the other half in order to form the actual cup. Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+function"} inverse function
            to this function is itself continuous, the torus and the coffee mug, both regarded as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} the same
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphic"} homeomorphic
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/Surfaces.png", :width => "400"}/
          %p
            On the other hand, there is
            %em no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
            to, for instance, the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
            of topological spaces (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+properties"}> topological properties
            ”) which allow to detect by means of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            manipulations whether two topological spaces are homeomorphic (or more generally
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            of a topological space (discussed
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#FundamentalGroups"} below
          %p
            Beware the popular imagery of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rubber-sheet+geometry"}> rubber-sheet geometry
            ”, which only captures part of the full scope of topology, in that it invokes spaces that
            %em locally
            still look like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            (called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+topological+spaces"} finite topological spaces
            are either
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"} discrete
            or very much unlike
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiniteT1SpacesAreDiscrete"}
            below); the former play a role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            one wishes to admit in the theory, extra “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"}> separation axioms
            ” are imposed on topological spaces (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#SeparationAxioms"} below
          %p
            Among the separation axioms, the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff space
            axiom is the most popular (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#TnTopologicalSpaces"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space"} sobriety
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SoberSpaces"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes+are+sober"}> schemes are sober
            ) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
            (
            %a{:href => "#Vickers89"}> Vickers 89
            ), and on the other, it fully realizes the strong roots that topology has in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+logic"} formal logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
            are entirely characterized by the union-, intersection- and inclusion-relations (logical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implication"} implication
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"}> propositions
            ). This leads to a natural and fruitful generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            to more general “purely logic-determined spaces”, called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            of mathematics and geometry provide an outlook on the relevance of the basic ideas of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In this first part we discuss the foundations of the concept of “sets equipped with topology” (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"}> topological spaces
            ) and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            between them.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #ClassicalLogic.un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"}> classical logic
                )
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
              in the following freely use the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+excluded+middle"} principle of excluded middle
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+by+contradiction"} proof by contradiction
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
            %p
              Hence we discuss
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              in its traditional form with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            %p
              We do however highlight the role of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              homomorphisms (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomomorphismOfFramesOfOpens"}
              below) and that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+spaces"} sober topological spaces
              (def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Sober"}
              below). These concepts pave the way to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
              formulation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
              in terms not of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              but in terms of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
              (remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Locales"}
              below). For further reading along these lines see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "locale#Johnstone83"} Johnstone 83
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"}> set theory
                )
            %p
              Apart from
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus S
                  of subsets;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                  sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(X)
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
                  sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(Y)
                  under a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∪
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\cup} S_i
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\cap} S_i
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} indexed sets of
                  subsets
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi i
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
            %p The only rules of set theory that we use are the
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions+of+images+and+pre-images+with+unions+and+intersections"} interactions of images and pre-images with unions and intersections
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"}> de Morgan duality
                  \.
            %p For reference, we recall these:
            #PreservationOfUnionsAndIntersectionsOfSets.num_prop
              %h6#proposition Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
                  preserve
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                  but not in general
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                between
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{S_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
                be a set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∪
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∪
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\left( \underset{i \in I}{\cup}  S_i\right) = \left(\underset{i \in I}{\cup} f(S_i)\right)
                    (the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                    under
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    of a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                    of subsets is the union of the images)
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\left( \underset{i \in I}{\cap}  S_i\right) \subset \left(\underset{i \in I}{\cap} f(S_i)\right)
                    (the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                    under
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                    of the subsets is contained in the intersection of the images).
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injection
                in the second item is in general proper. If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective function
                and if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} non-empty
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              %ul
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtext injective
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi S
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\,\text{injective}) \Rightarrow \left(f\left( \underset{i \in I}{\cap}  S_i\right) = \left(\underset{i \in I}{\cap} f(S_i)\right)\right)
            #PreservedByPreImages.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
                  preserve
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                between
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{T_i \subset Y\}_{i \in I}
                be a set of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∪
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∪
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}\left( \underset{i \in I}{\cup}  T_i\right) = \left(\underset{i \in I}{\cup} f^{-1}(T_i)\right)
                    (the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
                    under
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    of a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                    of subsets is the union of the pre-images),
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi i
                            %mo )
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo ∩
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi T
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}\left( \underset{i \in I}{\cap}  T_i\right) = \left(\underset{i \in I}{\cap} f^{-1}(T_i)\right)
                    (the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
                    under
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                    of the subsets is the intersection of the pre-images).
            #deMorgan.num_prop
              %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
              %p
                %strong
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan%27s+law"}> de Morgan's law
                  )
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and a set of subsets
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\{S_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              %p
                then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
                of their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                of their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∪
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ∩
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \setminus
                      \\left(
                      \\underset{i \in I}{\cup}  S_i
                      \\right)
                      \\;\;=\;\;
                      \\underset{i \in I}{\cap}
                      \\left(
                      X \setminus S_i
                      \\right)
              %p
                and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
                of their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                of their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \setminus
                      \\left(
                      \\underset{i \in I}{\cap}  S_i
                      \\right)
                      \\;\;=\;\;
                      \\underset{i \in I}{\cup}
                      \\left(
                      X \setminus S_i
                      \\right)
                      \\,.
              %p Moreover, taking complements reverses inclusion relations:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left(
                      S_1 \subset S_2
                      \\right)
                      \\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\,
                      \\left(
                      X\setminus S_2 \subset X \setminus S_1
                      \\right)
                      \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#Continuity Metric spaces
          %p
            The concept of continuity was first made precise in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epsilontic+analysis"} epsilontic analysis
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity"}
            below. Then it was realized that this has a more elegant formulation in terms of the more general concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+sets"} open sets
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuityBetweenMetricSpacesInTermsOfOpenSets"}
            below. Adopting the latter as the definition leads to a more abstract concept of “continuous space”, this is the concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSpace"}
            below.
          %p
            Here we briefly recall the relevant basic concepts from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#TopologicalSpaces"} Topological spaces
          #MetricSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"}> metric space
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  (the “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                  set”);
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \;\colon\; X \times X \to [0,\infty)
                  (the “distance function”) from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  of the set with itself to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonnegative+number"} non-negative
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %p
              such that for all
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in X
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (symmetry)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = d(y,x)
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"}> triangle inequality
                  )
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,z) \leq d(x,y)+ d(y,z)
              %li
                %p
                  (non-degeneracy)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = 0 \;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\; x = y
          #OpenBalls.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"}> open balls
                )
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in \mathbb{R}_+
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B^\circ_x(\epsilon)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    y \in X \;\vert\; d(x,y) \lt \epsilon
                    \\right\}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              around
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B_x(\epsilon)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    y \in X \;\vert\; d(x,y) \leq \epsilon
                    \\right\}
            %p
              for the
              %em closed ball
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              around
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_x(\epsilon)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    y \in X \;\vert\; d(x,y) = \epsilon
                    \\right\}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              around
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon = 1
              we also speak of the
              %em unit open/closed ball
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %em unit sphere
          #MetricSpaceBoundedSubset.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subset"} bounded subset
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is contained in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S \subset B^\circ_x(r)
            %p
              around some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              of some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{R}
          %p
            A key source of metric spaces are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} normed
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
          #NormedVectorSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (normed vector space)
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+space"} normed vector space
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  (the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        {\Vert {-} \Vert} \;\colon\; V \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
                %p
                  from the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-negative+number"} non-negative
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %p
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathbb{R}
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert c \vert}
              and all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v , w \in V
              it holds true that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (linearity)
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi c
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo =
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert c v \Vert} = {\vert c \vert} {\Vert v \Vert }
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"}> triangle inequality
                  )
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo +
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo ≤
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo +
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert v+w \Vert} \leq {\Vert v \Vert } + {\Vert w \Vert}
              %li
                %p
                  (non-degeneracy) if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert v \Vert} = 0
                  then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = 0
          #MetricSpaceFromNormedVectorSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+space"} normed vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, {\Vert {-} \Vert})
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d(x,y) \coloneqq {\Vert x-y \Vert}
                    \\,.
          %p
            Examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+spaces"} normed vector spaces
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormedVectorSpace"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpaceFromNormedVectorSpace"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            include the following:
          #EuclideanNorm.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"}> Euclidean space
                )
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    \\vec x
                    \=
                    (x_i)_{i = 1}^n
                    \\vert
                    x_i \in \mathbb{R}
                    \\right\}
            %p
              carries a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
              (the
              %em Euclidean norm
              ) given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/squares"} squares
              of the components:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msqrt
                      %mrow
                        %munderover
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\Vert \vec x \Vert}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\sqrt{
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{n}{\sum}
                    (x_i)^2
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Via prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpaceFromNormedVectorSpace"}
              this gives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              the structure of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #pNorm.num_defn
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Vector-p-Norms_qtl1.svg/220px-Vector-p-Norms_qtl1.svg.png", :width => "200"}/
            %p
              More generally, for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \geq 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              carries the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                    %mo ≔
                    %mroot
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mi i
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi p
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\Vert \vec x \Vert}_p  \coloneqq \root p {\sum_i {|x_i|^p}}
            %p One also sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi max
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\Vert \vec x \Vert}_\infty \coloneqq \underset{i \in I}{max} \, {\vert x_i \vert}
            %p
              and calls this the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum+norm"} supremum norm
            %p
              The graphics on the right (grabbed from Wikipedia) shows unit circles (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
              with respect to various
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norms"} p-norms
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+inequality"} Minkowski inequality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
              generalizes to non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
              such as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence+spaces"} sequence spaces
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+spaces"} Lebesgue spaces
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#ContinuityInAnalysis Continuity
          %p The following is now the fairly obvious definition of continuity for functions between metric spaces.
          #EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (epsilontic definition of continuity)
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/EpsilonDeltaBalls.png", :width => "250"}/
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d_X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,d_Y)
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
            %p
              is said to be
              %em
                continuous at a point
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \in X
              that are a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
              smaller than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              then their image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x')
              is a distance smaller than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              from
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext continuous at
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi x
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo &gt;
                            %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi δ
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mi δ
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi δ
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi ϵ
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    f\,\, \text{continuous at}\, x
                    \\right)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{{\epsilon \in \mathbb{R}} \atop {\epsilon \gt 0}}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{{\delta \in \mathbb{R}} \atop {\delta \gt 0}}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    \\left(
                    d_X(x,x') \lt \delta
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\Rightarrow\;\;
                    \\left(
                    d_Y(\,f(x), f(x')\,) \lt \epsilon
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is said to be
              %em continuous
              if it is continuous at every point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
          #DistanceFunctionFromsubset.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong (distance function from a subset is continuous)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of the underlying set. Define then the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d(S,-) \;\colon\; X \to \mathbb{R}
            %p
              from the underlying set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              by assigning to a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distances"} distances
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              ranges over the elements of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi inf
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d(S,x) \coloneqq inf \left\{ d(s,x) \,\vert\,  s\in S  \right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a continuous function, with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+norm"} Euclidean norm
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
            %p
              In particular the original distance function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,-) = d(\{x\},-)
              is continuous in both its arguments.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              be a positive real number. We need to find a positive real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) \lt \delta
              then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert d(S,x) - d(S,y) \vert} \lt \epsilon
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequalities"} triangle inequalities
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d(s,x) &amp; \leq d(s,y) + d(y,x)
                    \\\
                    d(s,y) &amp; \leq d(s,x) + d(x,y)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
              of all terms appearing here yields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    d(S,x) &amp; \leq d(S,y) + d(y,x)
                    \\\
                    d(S,y) &amp; \leq d(S,x) + d(x,y)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p which implies
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert d(S,x) - d(S,y) \vert} \leq d(x,y)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that we may take for instance
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \coloneqq \epsilon
          #PolynoialsAreContinuous.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions+are+continuous"}> rational functions are continuous
                )
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              regarded as the 1-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in \mathbb{R}[X]
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    f_P &amp;\colon&amp; \mathbb{R} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathbb{R}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; x &amp;\mapsto&amp; P(x)
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials+are+continuous+functions"} polynomials are continuous functions
            %p
              Similarly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions+are+continuous"} rational functions are continuous
              on their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              of definition: for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P,Q \in \mathbb{R}[X]
              two polynomials, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi Q
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{f_P}{f_Q} \colon \mathbb{R} \setminus \{x | f_Q(x) = 0\} \to \mathbb{R}
              is a continuous function.
            %p
              Also for instance forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
              is a continuous function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msqrt
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt(-) \colon \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
          %p
            On the other hand, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/step+function"} step function
            is continuous everywhere except at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
            of points at which it changes its value, see example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StepFunction"}
            below.
          %p
            We now reformulate the analytic concept of continuity from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity"}
            in terms of the simple but important concept of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+sets"} open sets
          #OpenSubsetsOfAMetricSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (neighbourhood and open set)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
                  of a point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi x
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \subset X
                  which contains some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_x^\circ(\epsilon) \subset U_x
                  around
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
                  such that for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
                  it also contains an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_x(\epsilon)
                  around
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
                  of a point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  which is also an open subset, hence equivalently this is any open subset of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  that contains
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            The following picture shows a point
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
            containing it, and two of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhoods"} neighbourhoods
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/NeighbourhoodsAndOpenBalls.png", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Munkres75"} Munkres 75
          #OpenEmptySet.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              %strong (the empty subset is open)
            %p
              Notice that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \subset X
              is always an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubsetsOfAMetricSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              says that “for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U
              there exists…”, but since there is no
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \emptyset
            %p
              Conversely, the entire set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is always an open subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
          #OpenAndClosedIntervals.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (open/closed
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intervals"} intervals
            %p
              Regard the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              as the 1-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b \in \mathbb{R}
              consider the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi x
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b) \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \lt x \lt b \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b] \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \lt x \leq b \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> half-open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi x
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,b) \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \leq x \lt b \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> half-open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,b] \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \leq x \leq b \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> closed interval
                  )
            %p
              The first of these is an open subset according to def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubsetsOfAMetricSpace"}
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+interval"} open interval
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
              and the middle two are called
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half-open+intervals"} half-open intervals
            %p
              Similarly for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b \in \mathbb{R}
              one considers
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\infty,b) \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert x \lt b  \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> unbounded open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi x
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,\infty) \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \lt x  \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,\,
                  (
                  %em> unbounded open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi x
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi b
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\infty,b] \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert x \leq b  \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  (
                  %em> unbounded half-open interval
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi x
                          %mo }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,\infty) \coloneqq \left\{ x \in \mathbb{R} \vert a \leq x  \right\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{AA}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,\,
                  (
                  %em> unbounded half-open interval
                  )
            %p The first two of these are open subsets, the last two are not.
            %p For completeness we may also consider
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\infty , \infty) = \mathbb{R}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,a) = \emptyset
            %p
              which are both open, according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSpace"}
          %p
            We may now rephrase the analytic definition of continuity entirely in terms of open subsets (def.
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubsetsOfAMetricSpace"}
          #ContinuityBetweenMetricSpacesInTermsOfOpenSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (rephrasing continuity in terms of open sets)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d_X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,d_Y)
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epsilontic+analysis"} epsilontic
              sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity"}
              precisely if it has the property that its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              (in the sense of def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubsetsOfAMetricSpace"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext continuous
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mi Y
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtext open
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi O
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mtext open
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    f \,\, \text{continuous}
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\;
                    \\left(
                    \\left(
                    O_Y \subset Y \,\, \text{open}
                    \\right)
                    \\,\Rightarrow\,
                    \\left(
                    f^{-1}(O_Y) \subset X \,\, \text{open}
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .un_remark{:style => "border:solid #0000cc;background: #add8e6;border-width:2px 1px;padding:0 1em;margin:0 1em;"}
            %p
              %strong principle of continuity
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
              %em Continuous pre-Images of open subsets are open.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Observe, by direct unwinding the definitions, that the epsilontic definition of continuity (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EpsilonDeltaDefinitionOfContinuity"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              precisely if for every open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon)
              around an image point, there exists an open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_x(\delta)
              around the corresponding pre-image point which maps into it:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi f
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext continuous at
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi x
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo ∀
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo &gt;
                                %mn 0
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo ∃
                                %mrow
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mo &gt;
                                  %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo ∘
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⊂
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi B
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi x
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ∘
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo ∀
                              %mrow
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo &gt;
                                %mn 0
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo ∃
                                %mrow
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mo &gt;
                                  %mn 0
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo ∘
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi δ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊂
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi B
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ∘
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ϵ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo )
                                %mo )
                              %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\left(
                    f \,\,\text{continuous at}\,\, x
                    \\right)
                    \&amp; \Leftrightarrow \;
                    \\underset{\epsilon \gt 0}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\delta \gt 0}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    f(\;B_x^\circ(\delta)\;) \;\subset\; B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \Leftrightarrow \;
                    \\underset{\epsilon \gt 0}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\delta \gt 0}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    B^\circ_x(\delta) \subset f^{-1}\left( B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon) \right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p With this observation the proof immediate. For the record, we spell it out:
            %p
              First assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous in the epsilontic sense. Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_Y \subset Y
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in f^{-1}(O_Y)
              any point in the pre-image, we need to show that there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi O
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(O_Y)
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_Y
              is open in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              means by definition that there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_Y
              around
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
              for some radius
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is continuous and using the above observation, this implies that there exists an open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_x(\delta)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(B^\circ_x(\delta)) \subset B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon) \subset Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi O
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_x(\delta) \subset f^{-1}\left(B^{\circ}_{f(x)}(\epsilon)\right) \subset f^{-1}(O_Y)
            %p
              Conversely, assume that the pre-image function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
              takes open subsets to open subsets. Then for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{f(x)}^\circ(\epsilon) \subset Y
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              around its image, we need to produce an open ball
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_x^\circ(\delta) \subset X
              around
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(B_x^\circ(\delta)) \subset B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon)
            %p
              But by definition of open subsets,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon) \subset Y
              is open, and therefore by assumption on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              its pre-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(B^\circ_{f(x)}(\epsilon)) \subset X
              is also an open subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #StepFunction.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/step+function"}> step function
                )
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/HeavisideFunction.png", :width => "300 /> "}/
            %p
              Consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              as the 1-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/step+function"} step function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi H
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℝ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mn 0
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                      %mi x
                                      %mo &gt;
                                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{R} &amp;\overset{H}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbb{R}
                    \\\
                    x
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; \vert \, x \leq 0
                    \\\
                    1 &amp; \vert \, x \gt 0
                    }
                    \\right.
                    }
                    \\,.
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from
                %a{:href => "#Vickers89"} Vickers 89
            %p
              Consider then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \lt b \in \mathbb{R}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+interval"} open interval
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b) \subset \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              according to example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenAndClosedIntervals"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{-1}(a,b)
              of this open subset is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
