          %p
            As a corollary of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urysohn%27s+lemma"} Urysohn's lemma
            we obtain yet another equivalent reformulation of the normality of topological spaces, this one now of a rather different character than the re-formulations in terms of explicit topological closures considered above:
          #NormalityEquivalentToUrysohnFunctionsExsist.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_23 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (normality equivalent to existence of Urysohn functions)
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-space" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
