          %p
            Further
            %a{:href => "#UniversalConstructions"} below
            we will see that, generally, among all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"} universal constructions
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            those that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            preserve the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
            property, while those that are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in general do not.
          %p
            But at least for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
