                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_2
            there is a universal way, called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflection
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffReflection"}
            below), to approximate any topological space “from the left” by a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
            topological spaces
          %p
            Hence if one wishes to work within the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            = succeed "-spaces" do
