          %h2#UniversalConstructions Universal constructions
          %p
            We have seen
            %a{:href => "#BasicConstructions"} above
            various construction principles for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BasicConstructions"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspaces"} topological subspaces
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quotient+spaces"} topological quotient spaces
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            into or out of these spaces, respectively (examples
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfBinaryProductSpace"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfDisjointUnionSpace"}
            and
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfQuotientSpace"}
            below).
          %p
            Since this is useful for handling topological spaces (we secretly used the universal property of the quotient space construction already in the proof of prop.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffReflectionViaHomsIntoAllHausdorffSpaces"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitingCone"}
            below, more general “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+constructions"}> universal constructions
            ” of topological spaces, called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of topological spaces (and to be distinguished from limits
            %em in
            topological spaces, in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} convergence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            as in def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Convergence"}
          %p
            Moreover, we have seen
            %a{:href => "#HausdorffReflections"} above
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
            construction in general does not preserve the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
