                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
            = succeed "-separated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoLimitsInNiceTopologicalSpaces"}
            below).
          %p
            After these general considerations, we finally discuss a
            %a{:href => "#UniversalConstructionsExamples"} list of examples
            of universal constructions in topological spaces.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            To motivate the following generalizations, first observe the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
            enjoyed by the basic construction principles of topological spaces from
            %a{:href => "#BasicConstructions"} above
          #UniversalPropertyOfBinaryProductSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_57 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
                of binary
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
