            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Often the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of a limit/colimit construction is all that one wants to know. But sometimes it is useful to have an explicit description of the limits/colimits, not the least because this proves that these actually exist. Here is the explicit description of the (co-)limiting cone over a diagram of sets:
          #SetLimits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_34 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "limits+and+colimits+by+example#limcoliminset"}> limits and colimits of sets
                )
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
