                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x'_i)_{i \in I}
            %p
              This shows that every cone with tip a singleton factors uniquely through the claimed limiting cone. But then for a cone with tip an arbitrary set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            It will turn out below in prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DescriptionOfLimitsAndColimitsInTop"}
            that limits and colimits of diagrams of topological spaces are computed by first applying prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SetLimits"}
            to the underlying diagram of underlying sets, and then equipping the result with a topology as follows:
          #InitialAndFinalTopologies.num_defn
            %h6#definition_34 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topology"} initial topology
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(X_i, \tau_i)\}_{i \in I}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a bare
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %ul
              %li
                %p For
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi S
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mi i
                            %mphantom
                              %mi AA
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{S \overset{\phantom{AA}p_i\phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow} X_i \}_{i \in I}
                %p
                  a set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                  out of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topology"} initial topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi initial
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{initial}(\{p_i\}_{i \in I})
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coarse+topology"} coarsest
                  topology on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InitialAndFinalTopologies"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi initial
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i \colon (S,\tau_{initial}(\{p_i\}_{i \in I})) \longrightarrow X_i
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
                %p
                  By lemma
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RecognizingTopologicalBasis"}
                  this is equivalently the topology whose open subsets are the unions of finite intersections of the preimages of the open subsets of the component spaces under the projection maps, hence the topology generated from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-base+for+a+topology"} sub-base
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi β
                          %mi ini
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
