                    \\,.
            %p
              If we
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choose
              one point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x'_n)
              in the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              this defines a sub-sequence, which converges to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %p
              In summary this proves that
              %em compact
              implies
              %em sequentially compact
              for metric spaces.
            %p
              For the converse, assume now that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,d)
              is sequentially compact. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
