          #OnePointExtensionWellDefined.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_19 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
                is well-defined)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              is indeed well defined in that the given set of subsets is indeed closed under arbitrary unions and finite intersections.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_81 Proof
            %p
              The unions and finite intersections of the open subsets inherited from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are closed among themselves by the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a topological space.
            %p It is hence sufficient to see that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the unions and finite intersection of the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo \
                        %mi CK
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  are closed among themselves,
              %li
                %p
                  the union and intersection of a subset of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %munder
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mtext open
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \underset{\text{open}}{\subset} X \subset X^\ast
                  with one of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo \
                        %mi CK
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  is again of one of the two kinds.
            %p
              Regarding the first statement: Under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∩
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %munder
                          %mi J
                          %mtext finite
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi CK
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∪
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %munder
                              %mi J
                              %mtext finite
                        %msub
                          %mi CK
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    i \in \underset{\text{finite}}{J}
                    }{\cap}
                    (X \backslash CK_i \cup \{\infty\})
                    \=
                    X \backslash
                    \\left(
                    \\left(\underset{i \in \underset{\text{finite}}{J}}{\cup} CK_i \right)
                    \\cup
                    \\{\infty\}
                    \\right)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi CK
                          %mi i
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\cup} ( X \backslash C_i \cup \{\infty\} )
                    \=
                    X \backslash
                    \\left(
                    \\left(\underset{i \in I}{\cap} CK_i \right)
                    \\cup
                    \\{\infty\}
                    \\right)
            %p
              and so the first statement follows from the fact that finite unions of compact subspaces and arbitrary intersections of closed compact subspaces are themselves again compact (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}
            %p
              Regarding the second statement: That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              is open means that there exists a closed subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset X
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = X\backslash C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
              we find
            %ol
              %li
                %p for intersections:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi U
                                %mo ∩
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∩
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi C
                                %mo ∪
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        U \cap ( (X\backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\} )
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash C) \cap (X \backslash CK)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; =
                        X \backslash ( C \cup CK )
                        \\end{aligned}
                %p
                  Since finite unions of closed subsets are closed, this is again an open subset of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p for unions:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi U
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi C
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mi CU
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo =
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo \
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi C
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi CK
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∪
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        U \cup (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash C) \cup (X \backslash CU) \cup \{\infty\}
                        \\\
                        \&amp; =
                        (X \backslash (C \cap CK)) \cup \{\infty\}
                        \\end{aligned}
                        \\,.
                %p
                  For this to be open in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
                  we need that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi CK
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \cap CK
                  is again compact. This follows because
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets+are+closed+in+a+closed+subspace+precisely+if+they+are+closed+in+the+ambient+space"} subsets are closed in a closed subspace precisely if they are closed in the ambient space
                  and because
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} closed subsets of compact spaces are compact
          #nSphereIsOnePointCompactificationOfRn.num_example
            %h6#example_104 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              with its standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              (e.g. as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
              with its
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^n \simeq (\mathbb{R}^n)^\ast
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_82 Proof
            %p
              Pick a point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty \in S^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stereographic+projection"} stereographic projection
              we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^n \setminus \{\infty\} \simeq \mathbb{R}^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              With this it only remains to see that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\infty \supset \{\infty\}
              an open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
              then the complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \setminus U_\infty
              is compact closed, and cnversely that the complement of every compact closed subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \setminus \{\infty\}
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\infty\}
            %p
              Observe that under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stereographic+projection"} stereographic projection
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StandardStereographicProjection"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\infty \setminus \{\infty\} \subset S^n \setminus \{\infty\}
              are identified precisely with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+subsets"} bounded subsets
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\infty\} \in S^n
              needs to contain an open ball around
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in \mathbb{R}^n \simeq S^n \setminus \{-\infty\}
              in the
              %em other
              stereographic projection, which under change of chart gives a bounded subset. )
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BorelHeine"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              are precisely the compact, and hence the compact closed, subsets of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \simeq S^n \setminus \{\infty\}
          %p
            The following are the basic properties of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
            in def.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
          #OnePointExtensionIsCompact.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_60 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
          .proof
            %h6#proof_83 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X^\ast\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %p That we have a cover means that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there must exist
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_\infty \in I
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mn ∞
                        %mo ⊃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i \infty} \supset \{\infty\}
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
                  of the extra point. But since, by construction, the only open subsets containing that point are of the form
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo \
                          %mi CK
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \backslash CK) \cup \{\infty\}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CK
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
                  with
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo \
                          %mi CK
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash CK \subset U_{i \infty}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in i}
                  is in particular an open cover of that closed compact subset
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CK
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset I
                  so that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} J
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \J \subset X}
                  is still a cover of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CK
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK
            %p Together this implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in J \subset I}
                    \\cup
                    \\{ U_{i_\infty} \}
            %p is a finite subcover of the original cover.
          #HausdorffOnePointCompactification.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_61 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
                of locally compact space is Hausdorff precisely if original space is)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_84 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is not Hausdorff then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              is not.
            %p
              For the converse, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is Hausdorff.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast = X \cup \{\infty\}
              as underlying sets, we only need to check that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              any point, then there is an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \subset X \subset X^\ast
              and an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\infty \subset X^\ast
              of the extra point which are disjoint.
            %p
              That
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is locally compact implies by definition that there exists an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_k \supset \{x\}
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CK
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \coloneqq Cl(U_x)
              is a closed compact neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CK
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \supset \{x\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_\infty \coloneqq (X \backslash CK ) \cup \{\infty\} \subset X^\ast
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\infty\}
              and the two are disjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_x \cap V_\infty = \emptyset
            %p by construction.
          #InclusionIntoOnePointExtensionIsOpenEmbedding.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_62 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (inclusion into
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
                is open
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow X^\ast
            %p
              into its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtension"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open map
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof_85 Proof
            %p
              Regarding the first point: For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              open and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CK
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CK \subset X
              closed and compact, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
              of the corresponding open subsets in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %mi CK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i^{-1}(U) = U
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    i^{-1}( (X \backslash CK) \cup \infty ) = X \backslash CK
            %p
              which are open in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Regarding the second point: The image of an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(U) = U \subset X^\ast
            %p
              Regarding the third point: We need to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon X \to i(X) \subset X^\ast
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
          %p As a corollary we finally obtain:
          #LocallyCompactHausdorffAreSubspacesOfCompactHausdorff.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_63 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+space"} locally compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
                are the open
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
              are, up to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              precisely the ope
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
          .proof
            %h6#proof_86 Proof
            %p
              That every open subspace of a compact Hausdorff space is locally compact Hausdorff was the statement of example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubspacesOfCompactHausdorffSpacesAreLocallyCompact"}
            %p
              But if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is locally compact Hausdorff, then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              is compact Hausdorff by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OnePointExtensionIsCompact"}
              and prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffOnePointCompactification"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow X^\ast
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as an open subspace of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionIntoOnePointExtensionIsOpenEmbedding"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            We close with two observations on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
            into locally compact spaces, which will be useful in the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embeddings+of+smooth+manifolds"} embeddings of smooth manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifolds"} below
          #ProperMapsToLocallyCompactSpacesAreClosed.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_64 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps+to+locally+compact+spaces+are+closed"}> proper maps to locally compact spaces are closed
                )
            %p Let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau_X)
                  be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                  (def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffTopologicalSpace"}
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper map
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProperContinuous"}
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenMap"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_87 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C) \subset Y
              is closed. By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionOfOpensGivesClosure"}
              this means we need to show that every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y \setminus f(C)
              has an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi y
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_y \supset \{y\}
              not intersecting
              = succeed ".." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C)
            %p
              By local compactness of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              has an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_y
              whose topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_y)
              is compact. Hence since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is proper, also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(Cl(V_y)) \subset X
              is compact. Then also the intersection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \cap f^{-1}(Cl(V_y))
              is compact, and since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+images+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} continuous images of compact spaces are compact
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ContinuousImageOfACompactSpaceIsCompact"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f\left( C \cap f^{-1}(Cl(V_y)) \right)
                    \=
                    f(C) \cap (Cl(V))
                    \\;
                    \\subset Y
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is also a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces+of+Hausdorff+spaces+are+closed"} compact subspaces of Hausdorff spaces are closed
              (lemma
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSubspacesOfHausdorffSpacesAreClosed"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi y
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi y
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_y \coloneqq V_y \setminus ( f(C) \cap (Cl(V_y)) ) = V_y \setminus f(C)
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              not intersecting
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(C)
          #InjectiveProperMapsAreEquivalentlyTheClosedEmbeddings.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_65 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+proper+maps+to+locally+compact+spaces+are+equivalently+the+closed+embeddings"}> injective proper maps to locally compact spaces are equivalently the closed embeddings
                )
            %p Let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau_X)
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
                  (def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffTopologicalSpace"}
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
                  be a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %p Then the following are equivalent
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper map
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a closed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfTopologicalSpaces"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_88 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an injective proper map, then since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps+to+locally+compact+spaces+are+closed"} proper maps to locally compact spaces are closed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+injections+are+embeddings"} closed injections are embeddings
              (prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenClosedContinuousInjectionsAreEmbeddings"}
            %p
              Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a closed embedding, we only need to show that the embedding map is proper. So for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset Y
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspace"} compact subspace
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(C) \subset X
              is also compact. But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an injection (being an embedding), that pre-image is just the intersection
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(C) \simeq C \cap f(X)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#ParacompactSpaces Paracompact spaces
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compactness
            in topology (
            %a{:href => "#CompactSpaces"}> above
            ) has several evident weakenings of interest. One is that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompactness
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
            below). The concept of paracompact topological spaces leads over from plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            to actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            discussed
            %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} below
            are paracompact topological spaces.
          %p
            A key property is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces
            are equivalently those (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffEquivalentToexistenceOfParititionsOfUnity"}
            below) all whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
            admit a subordinate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            below), namely a set of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            each of which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} supported
            in only one patch of the cover, but whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            is the unit function. Existence of such partitions implies that structures on topological spaces which are glued together via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+maps"} linear maps
            (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
          %p
            Finally in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            paracompact spaces are important as for them
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            may be computed in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #LocallyFiniteCover.num_defn
            %h6#definition_54 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"}> locally finite cover
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenCover"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is called
              %em locally finite
              if for all points
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              such that it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersects
              only finitely many elements of the cover, hence such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \cap U_i \neq \emptyset
              for only a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
          #RefinementOfOpenCovers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_55 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenCover"}
            %p
              Then a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              of this open cover is a set of open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_j \subset X\}_{j \in J}
              which is still an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              in itself and such that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in J
              there exists an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_j \subset U_i
          #ParacompactSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_56 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"}> paracompact topological space
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RefinementOfOpenCovers"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+open+cover"} locally finite open cover
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteCover"}
          %p
            Here are two basic classes of examples of paracompact spaces, below in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#ExamplesParacompactSpaces"} Examples
            we consider more sophisticated ones:
          #CompactSpaceIsParacompact.num_example
            %h6#example_105 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+spaces"} paracompact
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactTopologicalSpace"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
            %p Since a finite subcover is in particular a locally finite refinement.
          #ParacompactDisjointUnionOfParacompactSpaces.num_example
            %h6#example_106 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint unions
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+spaces"} paracompact spaces
                are paracompact)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(X_i, \tau_i)\}_{i \in I}
              be a set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+spaces"} paracompact topological spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DisjointUnionOfTopologicalSpaces"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} (X_i,\tau_i)
            %p is paracompact.
            %p
              In particular, by example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSpaceIsParacompact"}
              a non-finite disjoint union of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
              is, while no longer compact, still paracompact.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_89 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U} = \{ U_j \subset \underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} (X_i, \tau_i) \}_{j \in J}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %p
              Since each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
              is open in the disjoint union, the intersections
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \cap X_j
              are all open, and hence by forming all these intersections we obtain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              of the original cover by a disjoint union of open covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_i
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i, \tau_i)
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_i, \tau_i)
              is paracompact, each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_i
              has a locally finite refinement
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\sqcup}\mathcal{V}_i
              is a locally finite refinement of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In identifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces
            using the recognition principles that we establish
            %a{:href => "#ExamplesParacompactSpaces"} below
            it is often useful (as witnessed for instance by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact"}
            and prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularityConditionsForTopologicalManifoldsComparison"}
            below) to consider two closely related properties of topological spaces:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second-countability
                (def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CountableSecond"}
                below);
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compactness
                (def.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSigma"}
                below)
          #CountableSecond.num_defn
            %h6#definition_57 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"}> second-countable topological space
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second countable
              if it admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+a+topology"} base for its topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi β
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta_X
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyBase"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
              of open subsets.
          #SecondCountableEuclideanSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_107 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                is second-countable)
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+norm"} Euclidean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second countable
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CountableSecond"}
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} base open subsets
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^\circ_x(\epsilon)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in \mathbb{Q}_{\geq 0} \subset \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}
              and centered at points with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{Q}^n \subset \mathbb{R}^n
          .proof
            %h6#proof_90 Proof
            %p
              To see that this is still a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+a+topology"} base
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is contains in an open ball of rational radius with rational coordinates of its center that is still itself contained in the original open ball.
            %p
              To that end, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              be a point inside an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}
              be its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distance"} distance
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              of the ball. By the fact that the rational numbers are a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subset"} dense subset
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} epilon
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epilon \in \mathbb{Q}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt \epsilon \lt d/2
              and then we may find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \in \mathbb{Q}^n \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x' \in B_x^\circ(d/2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and is contained in the original open ball.
            %p To see that this base is countable, use that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the set of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  of two countable sets is countable.
          #CompactSigma.num_defn
            %h6#definition_58 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"}> sigma-compact topological space
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
              if it is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subsets"} compact subsets
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactTopologicalSpace"}
          #SigmaCompactEuclideanSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_108 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSigma"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_91 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K_k \coloneqq B_0(k) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+ball"} closed ball
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenBalls"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BorelHeine"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n = \underset{k \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} B_0(k)
                    \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#ExamplesParacompactSpaces Examples
          %p Below we consider three important classes of examples of paracompact spaces whose proof of paracompactness is non-trivial:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
                (prop.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactLocallyCompactTopologicalGroups"}
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
                (prop.
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactMetricSpace"}
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes"} CW-complexes
                (example
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffCWComplexes"}
          %p In order to discuss these, we first consider some recognition principles of paracompactness:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+second-countable+spaces+are+sigma-compact"} locally compact and second-countable spaces are sigma-compact
                (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SigmaCompactFromLocallyCompactAndSecondCountable"}
                below)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+sigma-compact+spaces+are+paracompact"} locally compact and sigma-compact spaces are paracompact
                (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact"}
                below)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+regular+spaces+are+paracompact"} second-countable regular spaces are paracompact
                (prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SecondCountableRegularSpacesAreParacompact"}
                below)
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtext second-countable
                            %mrow
                              %mi &amp;
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext locally compact
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtext second-countable
                            %mrow
                              %mi &amp;
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi regular
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi compact
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtext sigma-compact
                            %mrow
                              %mi &amp;
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mtext locally compact
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇘
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mtext paracompact
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; { \text{second-countable} \atop \&amp; \, \text{ locally compact } }
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \Downarrow
                  \\\
                  { \text{second-countable} \atop \&amp; \, { regular } }
                  \&amp;&amp; compact &amp;&amp; { \text{ sigma-compact } \atop \&amp; \, \text{locally compact} }
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \seArrow&amp; \Downarrow &amp; \swArrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;   \text{paracompact}
                  }
          %p
            More generally, these statements are direct consequences of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael%27s+theorem"} Michael's theorem
            on recognition of paracompactness (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularSpacesWherOpenCoveringIsRefinedbyCountableLocallyFiniteConnectionsofOpensAreParacompact"}
            below).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p The first of these statements is fairly immediate:
          #SigmaCompactFromLocallyCompactAndSecondCountable.num_prop
            %h6#lemma_20 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+second-countable+spaces+are+sigma-compact"}> locally compact and second-countable spaces are sigma-compact
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second-contable
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CountableSecond"}
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSigma"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_92 Proof
            %p
              We need to produce a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspaces"} compact subspaces
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second-countability
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+a+topology"} base
              of open subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\beta
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    B_i \subset X
                    \\right\}_{i \in I}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} local compactness
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              has an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_x)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %p
              By definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+a+topology"} base of a topology
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologyBase"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_x \in \beta
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x} \subset B_x \subset V_x
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(B_x) \subset Cl(V_x)
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets+are+closed+in+a+closed+subspace+precisely+if+they+are+closed+in+the+ambient+space"} subsets are closed in a closed subspace precisely if they are closed in the ambient space
              (lemma
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SubsetsInClosedSubspace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_x)
              is compact by assumption, and since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspaces+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} closed subspaces of compact spaces are compact
              (lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedSubsetsOfCompactSpacesAreCompact"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_x
              is compact.
            %p
              Applying this for each point exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as a union of compact closures of base opens:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X = \underset{x \in X}{\cup} Cl(B_x)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But since there is only a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
              of base open subsets to begin with, there is a countable subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset X
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X = \underset{x \in J}{\cup} Cl(B_x)
                    \\,.
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{Cl(B_x) \subset X\}_{x \in J}
            %p
              is a countable cover of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by compact subspaces.
          %p The other two statements need a little more preparation:
          #LocallyCompactAndSigmaCompactImpliesGoodNestedCover.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_21 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
                space admits nested countable cover by coompact subspaces)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactSigma"}
            %p
              Then there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+open+cover"} countable open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_i)
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosedSubset"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                  (def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactTopologicalSpace"}
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SubspaceTopology"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_i) \subset U_{i +1}
                  \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_93 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compactness
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{K_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 0
              set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_0 \coloneqq \emptyset
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then assume that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we have constructed a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}
              with the required properties.
            %p In particular this implies that the union
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Q_n \coloneqq Cl(U_n) \cup K_{n-1} \;\subset X
            %p
              is a compact subspace (by example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{n+1}
              of this union as follows:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_x \subset X\}_{x \in Q_n}
              be a set of open neighbourhood around each of the points in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} local compactness
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              there is a smaller open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtext compact
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{x\} \subset V_x \subset \underset{\text{compact}}{\Cl(V_x)} \subset U_x
                    \\,.
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_x \subset X\}_{x \in Q_n}
              is still an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_n \subset Q_n
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_x \subset X\}_{x \in J_n}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+open+cover"} finite open cover
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_{n + 1} \coloneqq \underset{x \in J_n}{\cup} V_x
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_n)
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOfAFiniteUnionIsUnionOfTheClosures"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{n+1}
              is compact:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cl
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi Cl
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo ∪
                                %mrow
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi J
                                    %mi n
                              %msub
                                %mi V
                                %mi x
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %munder
                              %mo ∪
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi J
                                  %mi n
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %mi Cl
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi V
                                  %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtext compact
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Cl(U_{n+1})
                    \&amp;=
                    Cl\left(  \underset{x\in J_n}{\cup} V_x \right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\underset{x \in J_n}{\cup} \underset{\text{compact}}{Cl( V_x )}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In conclusion, by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              we have produced a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_n \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_i)
              compact and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_i) \subset U_{i+1}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{n+1}
              is an open neighbourhood not just of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(U_{n})
              but in fact of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_n
              form a cover by assumption:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊃
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} U_i
                    \\supset
                    \\underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} K_i
                    \=
                    X
                    \\,.
          #ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_66 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+sigma-compact+spaces+are+paracompact"}> locally compact and sigma-compact spaces are paracompact
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"}> locally compact
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"}> sigma-compact
                  \.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
          .proof
            %h6#proof_94 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite cover
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactAndSigmaCompactImpliesGoodNestedCover"}
              there exists a countable open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_n \subset X\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_n)
                  is compact;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_n) \subset V_{n+1}
                  \.
            %p
              Notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1}) \setminus V_n
              is compact, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1})
              is compact and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_n
              is open, by example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IntersectionCompactWithOpen"}
            %p
              By this compactness, the cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              regarded as a cover of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1})\setminus V_n
              has a finite subcover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in J_n}
              indexed by a finite set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi n
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_n \subset I
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %p We consider the sets of intersections
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{U}_n
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\{ U_i \cap ( V_{n+2} \setminus Cl(V_{n-1}) )  \}_{i \in I}_{i \in J_n}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{n+2} \setminus Cl(V_{n-1})
              is open, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1}) \subset V_{n+2}
              by construction, this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_n
              is still an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∖
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1})\setminus V_n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{U} \coloneqq \underset{n\in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} \mathcal{U}_n
            %p is a locally finite refinement of the original cover, as required:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                  is a refinement, since by construction each element in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒰
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_n
                  is contained in one of the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                  is still a covering because by construction it covers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_{n+1}) \setminus V_n
                  for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi n
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_n \subset X\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                  also
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Cl(V_{n+1}) \setminus V_n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                  is a cover of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                  is locally finite because each point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  has an open neighbourhood of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{n+2} \setminus Cl(V_{n-1})
                  (since these also form an open cover, by the nestedness) and since by construction this has trivial intersection with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒰
                          %mrow
                            %mo ≥
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_{\geq n+3}
                  and since all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒰
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_n
                  are finite, so that also
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∪
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 3
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒰
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{k \lt n+3}{\cup} \mathcal{U}_k
                  is finite.
          %p Using this, we may finally demonstrate a fundamental example of a paracompact space:
          #ParacompactEuclideanSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_109 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_95 Proof
            %p
              The Euclidean space is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              by example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanSpacesAreLocallyCompact"}
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact+topological+space"} sigma-compact
              by example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SigmaCompactEuclideanSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+sigma-compact+spaces+are+paracompact"} locally compact and sigma-compact spaces are paracompact
              (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact"}
          %p
            More generally all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            are paracompact. This we consider below as prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactMetricSpace"}
          %p
            Using this recognition principle prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            (def.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactLocallyCompactTopologicalGroups"}
            below:
          #TopologicalGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_59 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"}> topological group
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi G
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_G \subset P(G)
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot (-)\;\colon\;G \times G \to G
              and the assignment of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+elements"} inverse elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1} : G \to G
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
          .num_example
            %h6#example_110 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
                as a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              and equipped with the addition operation from its canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              structure is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}^n, +)
          %p
            The following prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactLocallyCompactTopologicalGroups"}
            is a useful recognition principle for paracompact topological groups:
          #OpenSubgroupOfTopologicalGroupIsClosed.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_22 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (open subgroups of topological groups are closed)
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subset G
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
          .proof
            %h6#proof_96 Proof
            %p
              The set of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosets"} cosets
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subsets"} disjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              itself and hence it is the complement of the union of the other cosets, hence the complement of an open subspace, hence closed.
          #ParacompactLocallyCompactTopologicalGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_67 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyCompactSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_97 Proof
            %p
              By assumption of local compactness, there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e \subset G
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutral+element"} neutral element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in C_e
              any element, then also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inverse element
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{-1} \in C_e
            %p
              For if this is not the case, then we may enlarge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e
              by including its inverse elements, and the result is still a compact neighbourhood of the neutral element: Since taking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+elements"} inverse elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1} \colon G \to G
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+images+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} continuous images of compact spaces are compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e
              is compact, and the union of two compact subspaces is still compact (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}
            %p
              Now for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e^n  \subset G
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{k \in \{1, \cdots n\}}{\prod} C_e \subset \underset{k \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}{\prod} G
              under the iterated group product operation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ∈
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi G
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{k \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}{\prod} G \longrightarrow G
            %p Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H \coloneqq \underset{n \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} C_e^n
                    \\;\subset\;
                    G
            %p
              is clearly a topological subgroup of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p
              Observe that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e^n
              is compact. This is because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{k \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}{\prod}C_e
              is compact by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+theorem"} Tychonoff theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TychonoffTheorem"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+images+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} continuous images of compact spaces are compact
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H = \underset{n \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} C_e^n
            %p
              is a countable union of compact subspaces, making it
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-compact"} sigma-compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+and+sigma-compact+spaces+are+paracompact"} locally compact and sigma-compact spaces are paracompact
              (prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactFromLocallyCompactAndSigmacompact"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is paracompact.
            %p
              Observe also that the subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is open, because it contains with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_e
              a non-empty open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Int(C_e) \subset H
              and we may hence write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              as a union of open subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi H
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H = \underset{h \in H}{\cup} Int(C_e) \cdot h
                    \\,.
            %p
              Finally, as indicated in the proof of Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenSubgroupOfTopologicalGroupIsClosed"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              are all open and partition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DisjointUnionOfTopologicalSpaces"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  In the particular case where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnectedTopologicalSpace"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  itself. The argument above thus shows that a connected locally compact topological group is
                  = succeed "-compact" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %li
                %p
                  In the general case, all the cosets are homeomorphic to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  which we have just shown to be a paracompact group. Thus
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
                  of paracompact spaces. This is again paracompact by prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactDisjointUnionOfParacompactSpaces"}
          %p An archetypical example of a locally compact topological group is the general linear group:
          #GLn.num_example
            %h6#example_111 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"}> general linear group
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n, \mathbb{R})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
              is non-vanishing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ×
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi det
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left(
                    A \in Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R})
                    \\; \vert \;
                    det(A) \neq 0
                    \\right)
            %p
              with group operation given by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
            %p
              This becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_(n,\mathbb{R})
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SubspaceTopology"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi Mat
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n,\mathbb{R})\subset  Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R}) \simeq \mathbb{R}^{(n^2)}
            %p
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+function"} polynomial function
              and since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+matrix"} matrix inversion
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+function"} rational function
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials+are+continuous"} polynomials are continuous
              and more generally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions+are+continuous"} rational functions are continuous
              on their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              of definition (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynoialsAreContinuous"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ×
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R}) \subset Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              are indeed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
          %p
            There is another
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            which suggests itself on the general linear group: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
            (example
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactOpenTopology"}
          #AsSubspaceOfTheMappingSpace.num_example
            %h6#proposition_68 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
                of the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} mapping space
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              induced on the real general linear group when regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi Mat
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n,\mathbb{R})
                    \\subset
                    Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R})
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}^{(n^2)}
            %p
              (as in def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GLn"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(k^n, k^n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n,\mathbb{R})
                    \\subset
                    Maps(k^n, k^n)
            %p
              i.e. the set of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k^n \to k^n
              equipped with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
          .proof
            %h6#proof_98 Proof
            %p
              On the one hand, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalPropertyOfMappingSpace"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n, \mathbb{R}) \to Maps(\mathbb{R}^n, \mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of the defining continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n, \mathbb{R}) \times \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              is equal to or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finer+topology"} finer
              than the subspace topology coming from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Map
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(\mathbb{R}^n, \mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              We conclude by showing that it is also equal to or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coarser+topology"} coarser
            %p
              Since we are speaking about a subspace topology, we may consider the open subsets of the ambient Euclidean space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ×
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi n
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R}) \simeq \mathbb{R}^{(n^2)}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhood+base"} neighborhood base
              of a linear map or matrix
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              consists of sets of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mi A
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ×
                          %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_A^\epsilon
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{B \in Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R}) \,\vert\, \underset{{1 \leq i \leq n}}{\forall}\; |A e_i - B e_i| \lt \epsilon \right\}
            %p
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in (0,\infty)
            %p
              But this is also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+the+topology"} base
              element for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mi A
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msubsup
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_A^\epsilon
                    \\;=\;
                    \\bigcap_{i = 1}^n V_i^{K_i}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_i \coloneqq \{e_i\}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton"} singleton
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \coloneqq B^\circ_{A e^i}(\epsilon)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/radius"} radius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              around
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A e^i
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_69 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+topological+space"} paracompact Hausdorff
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GLn"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  not
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"}> locally compact
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+topological+space"}> paracompact Hausdorff
                  \.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_99 Proof
            %p Observe that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi Mat
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL_n(n,\mathbb{R}) \subset Mat_{n \times n}(\mathbb{R}) \simeq \mathbb{R}^{(n^2)}
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
              function (which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
              and hence continuous, example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynoialsAreContinuous"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \setminus \{0\} \subset \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi det
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(n,\mathbb{R}) = det^{-1}( \mathbb{R} \setminus \{0\} )
                    \\,.
            %p
              As an open subspace of Euclidean space,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              is not compact, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BorelHeine"}
            %p
              As Euclidean space is Hausdorff (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffMetricSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              of a Hausdorff space is again Hausdorff, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gl(n,\mathbb{R})
              is Hausdorff.
            %p
              Similarly, as Euclidean space is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanSpacesAreLocallyCompact"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              is locally compact.
            %p
              From this it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,\mathbb{R})
              is paracompact, since locally compact topological groups are paracompact by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactLocallyCompactTopologicalGroups"}
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Now we turn to the second recognition principle for paracompactness and the examples it implies. For the time being the remainded of this section is without proof. The reader may wish to skip ahead to the discussion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#PartitionsOfUnity"} Partitions of unity
          #RegularSpacesWherOpenCoveringIsRefinedbyCountableLocallyFiniteConnectionsofOpensAreParacompact.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_70 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael%27s+theorem"}> Michael's theorem
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+topological+space"} regular
              %li
                %p
                  every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
                  by a union of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+sets+of+subsets"} locally finite
                  sets of open subsets (the latter not necessarily covering).
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
          %p Using this one shows:
          #ParacompactMetricSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_71 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces+are+paracompact"}> metric spaces are paracompact
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              via its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
          #SecondCountableRegularSpacesAreParacompact.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_72 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+regular+spaces+are+paracompact"}> second-countable regular spaces are paracompact
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second-countable
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CountableSecond"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+topological+space"} regular
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalSpace"}
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
          .proof
            %h6#proof_100 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be an open cover. By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael%27s+theorem"} Michael's theorem
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegularSpacesWherOpenCoveringIsRefinedbyCountableLocallyFiniteConnectionsofOpensAreParacompact"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable cover
              (hence a countable union of sets consisting of single open subsets).
            %p But second countability implies precisely that every open cover has a countable subcover:
            %p
              Every open cover has a refinement by a cover consisting of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+for+the+topology"} base
              elements, and if there is only a countable set of these, then the resulting refinement necessarily contains at most this countable set of distinct open subsets.
          #ParacompactHausdorffCWComplexes.num_example
            %h6#example_112 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complexes+are+paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"}> CW-complexes are paracompact Hausdorff spaces
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+space"} paracompact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; S^{n-1} \longrightarrow X
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              from the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
              (with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              inherited from
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpheresAndDisks"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/attachment+space"} attachment space
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutInTop"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi f
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cup_f D^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                                %mi f
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi po
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi D
                                      %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ∪
                              %mi f
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{n-1} &amp;\overset{\phantom{A}f \phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{i_X}}
                    \\\
                    D^n &amp;\underset{i_{D^n}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \cup_f D^n
                    }
            %p is paracompact Hausdorff.
            %p
              This immediately implies that all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+CW-complexes"} finite CW-complexes
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelativeCellComplexes"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+space"} paracompact Hausdorff space
              are themselves paracompact Hausdorff. In fact this is true generally: all CW-complexes are paracompact Hausdorff spaces.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#PartitionsOfUnity Partitions of unity
          %p
            A key aspect of paracompact Hausdorff spaces is that they are equivalently those spaces that admit
            = succeed "." do
              %em partitions of unity
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            and prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffEquivalentToexistenceOfParititionsOfUnity"}
            below. The existence of partitions of unity on topological spaces is what starts to give them “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
            character”. For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            discussed
            %a{:href => "#VectorBundles"} below
            behave as expected in the presence of partitions of unity.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p Before we discuss partitions of unity, we consider some technical preliminaries on locally finite covers. First of all notice the following simple but useful fact:
          #LocallyFiniteRefinementInducesLocallyFiniteWithSameIndexSet.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_23 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (every locally finite refinement induces one with the original index set)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OpenCover"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_j \subset X\}_{j \in J}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RefinementOfOpenCovers"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite cover
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteCover"}
            %p
              By definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              we may
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choose
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \colon J \to I
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{j \in J}{\forall}\left( V_j \subset U_{\phi(j)} \right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\{ W_i \subset X \right\}_{i \in I}
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\underset{j \in \phi^{-1}(\{i\})}{\cup} V_j
                    \\right\}
            %p
              is still a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              to a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite cover
          .proof
            %h6#proof_101 Proof
            %p
              It is clear by construction that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_i \subset U_i
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/refinement"} refinement
            %p
              Hence consider
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi j
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_j \subset X\}_{j \in J}
              is locally finite, it follows that there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset J
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{j \in J\setminus K}{\forall} \left( U_x \cap V_j = \emptyset \right)
                    \\,.
            %p Hence by construction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I\setminus \phi(K)}{\forall} \left( U_x \cap W_i = \emptyset \right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(K) \subset I
              is still a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is locally finite.
          %p
            In the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} below
          #ParacompactHausdorffSpacesAreNormal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_73 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"}> paracompact Hausdorff spaces are normal
                )
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+space"} paracompact Hausdorff space
              (def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffTopologicalSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+Hausdorff+space"} normal
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalSpace"}
            %p
              In particular
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} compact Hausdorff spaces are normal
          .proof
            %h6#proof_102 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a paracompact Hausdorff space
            %p
              We first show that it is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+topological+space"} regular
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              be a point, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed subset
              not containing
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi C
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C \supset C
            %p
              First of all, by the Hausdorff property there exists for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              disjoint open neighbourhoods
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{x,c} \supset \{x\}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi c
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_c \supset \{c\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              ranges, the latter clearly form an open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_c \subset X\}_{c \in C}
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{U_c \subset X\}_{c \in C} \,\cup\, X \setminus C
            %p
              is an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteRefinementInducesLocallyFiniteWithSameIndexSet"}
              we may assume its elements to share the original index set and be contained in the original elements of the same index. Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{V_c \subset U_c \subset  X\}_{c \in C}
            %p is a locally finite collection of subsets, such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi C
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_C \coloneqq \underset{c \in C}{\cup} V_c
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Now by definition of local finiteness there exists an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_x \supset \{x\}
              and a finite subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset C
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{c \in C \setminus K}{\forall}( W_x \cap V_c = \emptyset )
                    \\,.
            %p Consider then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∩
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi K
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi k
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_x
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    W_x
                    \\cap
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{k \in K}{\cap}
                    \\left(
                    U_{x,k}
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p It thus only remains to see that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_x \cap U_C = \emptyset
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this holds because the only
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{c}
              that intersect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_x
              are the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{k} \subset U_{k}
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in K
              and each of these is by construction disjoint from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{x,k}
              and hence from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
            %p
              This establishes that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is regular. Now we prove that it is normal. For this we use the same approach as before:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C,D \subset X
              be two disjoint closed subsets. By need to produce disjoint open neighbourhoods for these.
            %p
              By the previous statement of regularity, we may find for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              disjoint open neighbourhoods
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_c \subset \{c\}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %mi c
                      %mo ⊃
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{D,c} \supset D
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi c
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    U_c \subset X
                    \\right\}_{c \in C}
                    \\cup
                    X \setminus C
            %p
              is an open cover of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteRefinementInducesLocallyFiniteWithSameIndexSet"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ V_c \subset U_c \subset X \}_{c \in C}
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi C
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_{C}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{c \in C}{\cup} V_c
            %p
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              It is now sufficient to see that every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              has an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_d
              not intersecting
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi D
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_D \coloneqq \underset{d \in D}{\cup} U_d
            %p
              is the required open neighbourhood of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              not intersecting
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C
            %p
              Now by local finiteness of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi c
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_c \subset X\}_{c \in X}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
              has an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_d
              such that there is a finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi d
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_d \subset C
              so that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∖
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mi d
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi c
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{c \in C \setminus K_d}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    V_c \cap W_d = \emptyset
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p Accordingly the intersection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi d
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi d
                    %mo ∩
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∩
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi d
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %mi c
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U_d
                    \\coloneqq
                    W_d
                    \\cap
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{c \in K_d \subset C}{\cap} U_{D,c}
                    \\right)
            %p
              is still open and disjoint from the remaining
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_k
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_C
          %p
            That paracompact Hausdorff spaces are normal (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffSpacesAreNormal"}
          #PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_24 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
                for locally finite covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NormalSpace"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteCover"}
            %p
              Then there exists another open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_i)
              of its elements is contained in the original patches:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          %p
            We now
            %strong prove
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
            in increasing generality; first for binary open covers (lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
            below), then for finite covers (lemma
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForLocallyFiniteCountableCovers"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          #ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_25 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
                for binary covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U \subset X\}_{i \in \{1,2\}}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              by two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            %p
              Then there exists an open set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset X
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \subset Cl(V_1) \subset U_1
            %p
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_1,U_2\}
              is still an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof_103 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cup U_2 = X
              it follows (by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan%27s+law"} de Morgan's law
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#deMorgan"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus U_i
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subset"} disjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              there exist disjoint open subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \supset X \setminus U_2
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    V_2 \supset X \setminus U_1
                    \\,.
            %p By their disjointness, we have the following inclusions:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \subset X \setminus V_2 \subset U_1
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus V_2
              is closed, this means that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∖
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_1) \subset Cl(X \setminus V_2) =  X \setminus V_2
            %p
              Hence it only remains to observe that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \cup U_2 = X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1
          #ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_26 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
                for finite covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              of patches. Then there exists another open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
          .proof
            %h6#proof_104 Proof
            %p
              By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
            %p
              To begin with, consider
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %munderover
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ U_1, \underoverset{i = 2}{n}{\cup} U_i\}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
              gives an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset Cl(V_1) \subset U_1
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_1, \underoverset{i = 2}{n}{\cup} U_i\}
              is still an open cover, and accordingly so is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ V_1  \} \cup \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i \in \{2, \cdots, n\}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Similarly we next find an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 \subset Cl(V_2) \subset U_2
              and such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ V_1, ,V_2  \} \cup \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i \in \{3, \cdots, n\}}
            %p
              is an open cover. After
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              such steps we are left with an open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}
              as required.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_22 Remark
            %p
              Beware the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              in lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
              does
              %em not
              give the statement for infinite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+covers"} countable covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} V_i
              is a cover.
            %p
              And in fact, assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dowker+space"} Dowker space
              due to
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Beslagic85"} Beslagic 85
          %p
            This issue is evaded if we consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+covers"} locally finite
            countable covers:
          #ShrinkingLemmaForLocallyFiniteCountableCovers.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_27 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
                for locally finite countable covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable cover
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset X
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              is still a cover.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_105 Proof
            %p
              As in the proof of lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              and such that for every finite number, hence every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underoverset{i = 0}{n}{\cup} V_i
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underoverset{i = 0}{n}{\cup} U_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now the extra assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              implies that every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              is contained in only finitely many of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_x \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in \underoverset{i = 0}{n_x}{\cup} U_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that for every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in \underoverset{i = 0}{n_x}{\cup} V_i
                    \\subset \underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} V_i
            %p
              hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              is indeed a cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is as far as one gets without the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
            to generalize the shrinking lemma for finitely many patches (lemma
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_106 Proof
            %p
              of the general
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be the given locally finite cover of the normal space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              consisting of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset I
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} = \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
            %p with the property that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \in J \subset I) \Rightarrow ( Cl(V_i) \subset U_i )
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \in I \setminus J) \Rightarrow ( V_i = U_i )
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
                  is an open cover of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Equip the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
              by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒲
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext and
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi J
                              %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    (J_1, \mathcal{V})
                    \\leq
                    (J_2, \mathcal{W})
                    \\right)
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\left(
                    \\left(
                    J_1 \subset J_2
                    \\right)
                    \\,\text{and}\,
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{i \in J_1}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    V_i = W_i
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By definition, an element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
              is an open cover of the required form.
            %p
              We claim now that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
            %p
              For assume on the contrary that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              is maximal and there were
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I \setminus J
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
              to replace that single
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
              with a smaller open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'_i
              to obtain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}'
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V'_i) \subset V_i
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}'
              is still an open cover. But that would mean that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V}) \lt (J \cup \{i\}, \mathcal{V}')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              is maximal. This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+by+contradiction"} proves by contradiction
              that a maximal element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
              and hence is an open cover as required.
            %p
              We are reduced now to showing that a maximal element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              exists. To achieve this we invoke
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              has an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bound"} upper bound
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset S
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered
              subset. Consider the union of all the index sets appearing in the pairs in this subset:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                    %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{(J,\mathcal{V}) \in T  }{\cup} J
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now define open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K
              picking any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in J
              and setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i \coloneqq V_i \phantom{AAA} i \in K
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is independent of the choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\leq)
              is totally ordered.
            %p
              Moreover, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I\setminus K
              define
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i \coloneqq U_i  \phantom{AAA} i \in I \setminus K
                    \\,.
            %p
              We claim now that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              thus defined is a cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is locally finite, so for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              there exists a finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x \subset I
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                      %mo ∖
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∉
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \in I \setminus J_x) \Rightarrow (x \notin U_i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\leq)
              is a total order, it must contain an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              such that the finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x \cap K
              is contained in its index set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x \cap K \subset J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              is a cover, it follows that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi x
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \underset{i \in J_x \cap K}{V_i} \subset  \underset{i \in I}{\cup} V_i
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\cup} W_i
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (K,\mathcal{W})
              is indeed an element of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T ,\leq )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has an upper bound, and so Zorn’s lemma implies the claim.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p After these preliminaries, we finally turn to the partitions of unity:
          #PartitionOfUnity.num_defn
            %h6#definition_60 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"}> partition of unity
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
                subordinate to the cover
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\}_{i \in I}
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f_i \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow [0,1]
                %p
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi ℝ
