          #RemarkPartitionOfUnity.num_remark
            %h6#remark_23 Remark
            %p
              Regarding the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Due to the second clause in def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
                  in the third clause involves only a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
                  of elements not equal to zero, and therefore is well defined.
              %li
                %p
                  Due to the third clause, the interiors of the supports
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %msubsup
                              %mi h
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi X
                            %mo }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left \{ h_i^{-1}( (0,1] ) \subset X \right\}_{i \in I}
                  constitute a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      they are open, since they are the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
                      under the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
                      of the open subset
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ⊂
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1] \subset [0,1]
                  %li
                    %p
                      they cover because, by the third clause, for each
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi x
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in x
                      there is at least one
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
                      with
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi h
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mn 0
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_i(X) \gt 0
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ∈
                            %msubsup
                              %mi h
                              %mi i
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in h_i^{-1}((0,1])
                  %li
                    %p they are locally finite because by the second clause already their closures are locally finite.
          #PartitionOfUnityOnTheRealLine.num_example
            %h6#example_113 Example
            %p
              Consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in (0,\infty)
              and consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{
                    (n-1-\epsilon , n+1 +  \epsilon) \subset \mathbb{R}
                    \\}_{n \in \mathbb{Z} \subset \mathbb{R} }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ f_n \colon \mathbb{R} \to [0,1] \}_{n \in \mathbb{Z}}
              (def.
              = succeed "))" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi x
                              %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi x
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo −
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi x
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_n(x)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    x - (n - 1)  &amp;\vert&amp; n - 1 \leq x \leq n
                    \\\
                    1- (x-n) &amp;\vert&amp; n \leq x \leq n+1
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
          #ParacompactHausdorffEquivalentToexistenceOfParititionsOfUnity.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_74 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+equivalently+admit+subordinate+partitions+of+unity"}> paracompact Hausdorff spaces equivalently admit subordinate partitions of unity
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HausdorffTopologicalSpace"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactSpace"}
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi τ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
                  admits a subordinate
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
          #OpenCoverOfParacompactHausdorffSpaceAdmitsPartitionOfUnityProof.proof
            %h6#proof_107 Proof
            %p
              One direction is immediate: Assume that every open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              admits a subordinate partition of unity
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i\}_{i \in I}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Int
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ Int(Supp(f)_i)  \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is a locally finite open cover refining the original one (remark
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkPartitionOfUnity"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is paracompact.
            %p
              We need to show the converse: If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              there is a subordinate
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            %p
              By paracompactness of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFiniteRefinementInducesLocallyFiniteWithSameIndexSet"}
              we may assume that this has the same index set. It is now sufficient to show that this locally finite cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              admits a subordinate partition of unity, since this will then also be subordinate to the original cover.
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces are normal
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffSpacesAreNormal"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shrinking+lemma"} shrinking lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
              to the given locally finite open cover
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    W_i \subset Cl(W_i) \subset V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              It follows that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
              we have two disjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(W_i)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \setminus V_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cl(W_i) \cap (X\setminus V_i) = \emptyset
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+normal"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces are normal
              (prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffSpacesAreNormal"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urysohn%27s+lemma"} Urysohn's lemma
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UrysohnLemma"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h_i \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow [0,1]
            %p with the property that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h_i( Cl(W_i) ) = \{1\}
                    \\,,
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    h_i( X \setminus V_i ) = \{0\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means in particular that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_i^{-1}((0,1]) \subset V_i
              and hence that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support"} support
              of the function is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Supp(h_i) =  Cl(h_i^{-1}((0,1])) \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              By this construction, the set of function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{h_i\}_{i \in I}
              already satisfies conditions 1) and 2) on a partition of unity subordinate to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow [0,1]
            %p
              defined on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    h(x) \coloneqq \underset{i \in I}{\sum} h_i(x)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
              on the right has only a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              of non-zero summands, due to the local finiteness of the cover, so that this is well-defined. Moreover this is again a continuous function, since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomials+are+continuous"} polynomials are continuous
              (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynoialsAreContinuous"}
            %p Moreover, notice that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{x \in X}{\forall} \left(  h(x) \neq 0  \right)
            %p
              because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{Cl(W_i) \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is a cover so that there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_x \in I
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in Cl(W_{i_x})
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_i(Cl(W_{i_x})) = \{1\}
            %p
              Hence it makes sense to define the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ratios"} ratios
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi h
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_i \;\coloneqq\;  h_i/h
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Supp(f_i) = Supp(h_i)
              this still satisfies conditions 1) and 2) on a partition of unity (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartitionOfUnity"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\sum} f_i = 1
            %p and hence the remaining condition 3). Therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left\{
                    f_i
                    \\right\}_{i \in I}
            %p is a partition of unity as required.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            We will see various applications of prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffEquivalentToexistenceOfParititionsOfUnity"}
            in the discussion of
            %a{:href => "#VectorBundles"} topological vector bundles
            and of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} topological manifolds
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#VectorBundles Vector bundles
          %p
            A
            %em
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"}> topological
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            is a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            that vary continuously over a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+spaces"} tensor product of vector spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus_X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_X
            on vector bundles over some base space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DirectSumOfTopologicalVectorBundlesViaTransitionFunctions"}
            and def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductOfVectorBundles"}
            below).
          %p
            This way a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-ring"} semi-ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim}, \oplus_X, \otimes_X)
            of isomorphism classes of topological vector bundles is associated with every
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} group completion
            of the direct sum of vector bundles) one obtains an actual ring, called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            of the topological space. This is a fundamental topological invariant that plays a central role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
          %p
            A key class of examples of topological vector bundles are the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
            to which we turn
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} below
          %p
            Topological vector bundles are particularly well behaved over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partitions+of+unity"} partitions of unity
            (by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParacompactHausdorffEquivalentToexistenceOfParititionsOfUnity"}
            above) allows to perform global operations on vector bundles by first performing them locally and then using the partition of unity to continuously interpolate between these local constructions. This is one reason why the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifolds"} topological manifolds
            %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} below
            demands them to be paracompact Hausdorff spaces.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The combination of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            begins in the evident way, in the same vein as the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            (def.
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            (remark
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopCategory"}
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartesianSymmetricMonoidalTop"}
          #TopologicalRing.num_defn
            %h6#definition_61 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,+,\cdot)
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi R
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_R \subset P(R)
                  on the underlying set of the ring, making it a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,\tau_R)
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSpace"}
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,+)
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                  with respect to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_R
                  (def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalGroup"}
              %li
                %p
                  also the multiplication
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi R
                        %mo ×
                        %mi R
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\cdot (-) \;\colon\; R \times R \longrightarrow R
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                  with respect to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_R
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
                  (example
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BinaryProductTopologicalSpace"}
            %p
              A topological ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((R, \tau_R),+,\cdot)
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (R,+,\cdot)
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %li
                %p
                  the function assigning multiplicative inverses
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∖
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∖
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1} \;\colon\; R \setminus \{0\} \to R \setminus \{0\}
                  is a continuous function with respect to the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_24 Remark
            %p
              There is a redundancy in def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRing"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+ring"} topological ring
              the continuity of the assignment of additive inverses is already implied by the continuity of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplication"} multiplication
              operation, since
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \- a = (-1) \cdot a
                    \\,.
          #TopologicalRingRealNumbers.num_example
            %h6#example_114 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+fields"} topological fields
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              and of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C} \simeq \mathbb{R}^2
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+fields"} topological fields
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRing"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
              (example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EuclideanNorm"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MetricTopology"}
            %p
              That the operations on these fields are all continuous with respect to the Euclidean topology is the statement that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+functions+are+continuous"} rational functions are continuous
              on the domain of definition inside Euclidean space (example
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynoialsAreContinuous"}
          #TopologicalVectorBundle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_62 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"}> topological vector bundle
                )
            %p Let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalRing"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  be a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %p
              Then a
              %em
                topological
                = succeed "-vector" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi π
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \overset{\pi}{\to} X
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  the structure of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi x
                        %mo ≔
                        %msup
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_x \coloneqq \pi^{-1}(\{x\}) \subset E
                %p
                  called the
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                  of the bundle over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %p
              such that this is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+trivialization"} locally trivial
              in that there exists:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
                  an
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_i \in \mathbb{N}
                  and a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi k
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi i
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi_i \;\colon\; U_i \times k^{n_i} \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \pi^{-1}(U_i) \subset E
                %p
                  from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                  with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  to the restriction of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
                      is a function over
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                      in that
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi π
                              %mo ∘
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %msub
                                %mi pr
                                %mn 1
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \circ \phi_i = pr_1
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi k
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊂
                            %msup
                              %mi π
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i(\{x\} \times k^n) \subset \pi^{-1}(\{x\})
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi i
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
                      is a
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                      in each fiber in that
                    .maruku-equation
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo ∀
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mi i
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %msup
                                %mi k
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi n
                                    %mi i
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mtext linear
                              %msub
                                %mi E
                                %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %msup
                                %mi π
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            \\underset{x \in U_i}{\forall}
                            \\left(
                            \\phi_i(x) \;\colon\;
                            k^{n_i} \overset{\text{linear}}{\longrightarrow}
                            E_x = \pi^{-1}(\{x\})
                            \\right)
                            \\,.
            %p
              Here is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of continuous functions that illustrates these conditions:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi k
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mtext fibws. linear
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
