          #TopologicalVectorBundlesCategory.num_remark
            %h6#remark_25 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect%28X%29"}> category of topological vector bundles
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are the topological
                  = succeed "-vector" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are the topological
                  = succeed "-vector" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalVectorBundle"}
            %p#NotationForCategoryOfVectorBundles
              This category is usually denoted
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect_k(X)
              or just
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect%28X%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)
              when the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              is understood (often: the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %p
              The set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              in this category (topological vector bundles modulo invertible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              between them) we denote by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)_{/\sim}
            %p
              There is a larger category, where we allow the morphisms to involve a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              between base spaces, so that the continuous functions on total spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon E_1 \longrightarrow E_2
              are, besides being fiberwise linear, required to make the following diagram commute:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi π
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi π
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E_1 &amp;\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; E_2
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\pi_1}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\pi_2}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\underset{\tilde f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    }
                    \\,.
