            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+space"} locally Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyEuclideanSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComponentsConnected"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected components
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PathConnectedComponents"}
          %p But the “global” topological properties of Euclidean space are not generally inherited by locally Euclidean spaces. This sounds obvious, but notice that also Hausdorff-ness is a “global property”:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_30 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (locally Euclidean spaces are not necessarily
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_2
            %p
              It might superficially seem that every locally Euclidean space (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyEuclideanSpace"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            %p
              But this is not so, see the counter-example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NonHausdorffManifolds"}
              below, Hausdorffness is a “non-local condition”, as opposed to the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axioms"} separation axioms
          #NonHausdorffManifolds.num_example
            %h6#nonexample_3 Nonexample
            %p
              %strong
