                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(T X)
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
              of tangent vector fields on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_37 Remark
            %p
              %strong (notation for tangent vectors in a chart)
            %p
              Under the bijection of lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearTangentSpace"}
              one often denotes the tangent vector corresponding to the the
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} basis
              vector of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mtext or just
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\frac{\partial}{\partial x^i}
                    \\phantom{AA} \text{or just } \phantom{AA}
                    \\partial_i
            %p
              because under the identification of tangent vectors with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
              on the algebra of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+functions"} differentiable functions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              as
              %a{:href => "#AlgebraicDefinition"} above
              then it acts as the operation of taking the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \mathbb{R}^n
              is then denoted by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mtext or just
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{n}{\sum}
                    v^i
                    \\frac{\partial}{\partial x^i}
                    \\phantom{AA} \text{or just } \phantom{AA}
                    \\underoverset{i = 1}{n}{\sum} v^i \partial_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Notice that this identification depends on the choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
            %p
              Sometimes, notably in texts on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermodynamics"} thermodynamics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
              on a 2-dimensional manifold are used as coordinate functions for a local chart (i.e. so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^1 = f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^2 = g
              ), then one writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi g
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AA
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi g
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\partial/\partial f)_g
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    (\partial/\partial g)_f
            %p
              for the tangent vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\partial}{\partial x^1}
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mo ∂
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mn 2
