          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifolds Embeddings
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+topological+spaces"} embedding of topological spaces
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfTopologicalSpaces"}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedding of smooth manifolds
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothManifoldsEmbedding"}
            below) is similarly meant to be an an inclusion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
            induces the included one. In order for this to be the case we need that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+spaces"} tangent spaces
            include into each other. This is the concept of an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion+of+differentiable+manifolds"} immersion of differentiable manifolds
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Immersion"}
            below).
          %p
            It turns out that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            embeds this way into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            manifolds and without any bound on the dimension of the ambient Euclidean space) below as prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactManifoldEmbedsIntoLargeDimensionalEuclideanSpace"}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+embedding+theorem"} Whitney embedding theorem
            (remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingWhitney"}
            below).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #Immersion.num_defn
            %h6#definition_87 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion+of+differentiable+manifolds"} immersion
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion+of+differentiable+manifolds"} submersion of differentiable manifolds
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
